# Planar Void's "whenever another card is put into a graveyard from anywhere" is never a leaves-the-battlefield ability
# (CR 603.6c), so it doesn't look back in time (CR 603.10a): it is judged on the board after the event, and a Hushbringer
# dying at the same time as the creatures no longer stops anything (Hushbringer's rulings: a "from anywhere" ability
# triggers if Hushbringer leaves the battlefield at the same time). Bot1 casts Planar Void, Ornithopter and Hushbringer on
# turn 1; on turn 3 Pyroclasm kills Hushbringer and the Ornithopter together, and the Void exiles both and the Pyroclasm
# (and the Island Bot2 discarded to hand size on turn 2).

